WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.791 --> 00:00:30.625
In the previous

2
00:00:30.625 --> 00:00:33.958
verses of Chapter 16, Lord Krishna warned –

3
00:00:33.958 --> 00:00:37.166
kamah, that is, lust, krodhah,

4
00:00:37.166 --> 00:00:40.333
and lobhah are the three gateways to hell.

5
00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:44.041
Now He moves from warning to assurance.

6
00:00:44.041 --> 00:00:45.291
The question is –

7
00:00:45.291 --> 00:00:48.416
when a seeker escapes these gateways,

8
00:00:48.416 --> 00:00:50.250
when they give up lust, anger,

9
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.708
and greed,

10
00:00:52.708 --> 00:00:54.833
what happens to them?

11
00:00:59.375 --> 00:01:01.708
In this verse Lord Krishna says –

12
00:01:01.708 --> 00:01:03.250
the seeker who is

13
00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:07.208
etaih vimuktah, freed from
these three darkness-gateways,

14
00:01:07.208 --> 00:01:08.875
that is, lust, anger,

15
00:01:08.875 --> 00:01:12.500
and greed, acharaty-

16
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.541
atmanah shreyah, that is, acts for the soul's

17
00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:18.916
welfare, and going forward, tato

18
00:01:18.916 --> 00:01:20.583
yati param gatim,

19
00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:21.500
gradually

20
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.041
reaches the supreme state, that is, liberation.

21
00:01:25.041 --> 00:01:27.958
Tamo-dvaraih, the gateways of darkness.

22
00:01:27.958 --> 00:01:30.125
This metaphor is used again here.

23
00:01:30.125 --> 00:01:31.083
Just as a door

24
00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:33.250
leads us to a place,

25
00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:36.333
in the same way lust, anger, and greed

26
00:01:36.333 --> 00:01:40.208
lead the seeker toward spiritual blindness.

27
00:01:40.208 --> 00:01:43.000
But if one does not step through them at all,

28
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.208
this darkness lifts.

29
00:01:46.208 --> 00:01:48.416
Etaih vimuktah

30
00:01:48.416 --> 00:01:52.000
signals that freedom from these is possible.

31
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.041
These are not eternal bondages,

32
00:01:54.041 --> 00:01:57.458
but nets formed by circumstance.

33
00:01:57.458 --> 00:02:02.125
Arising from desire, reaction, and attachment.

34
00:02:02.125 --> 00:02:05.208
The seeker can recognise and release them.

35
00:02:05.208 --> 00:02:07.583
When selfishness and distortion are removed,

36
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:11.166
acharatyatmanah shreyah, that is,

37
00:02:11.166 --> 00:02:15.166
the seeker's conduct naturally
becomes aligned with dharma.

38
00:02:15.166 --> 00:02:17.166
They spontaneously connect with truth

39
00:02:17.166 --> 00:02:19.791
and wellbeing.

40
00:02:19.791 --> 00:02:23.166
And finally, tato yati param gatim,

41
00:02:23.166 --> 00:02:26.083
that is, the supreme state is reached.

42
00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:27.500
This is moksha.

43
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.791
Liberation from the cycle of birth and death.

44
00:02:30.791 --> 00:02:33.125
The message of this verse is clear:

45
00:02:33.125 --> 00:02:34.125
the path to liberation

46
00:02:34.125 --> 00:02:36.416
does not begin with some mysterious practice,

47
00:02:36.416 --> 00:02:40.000
but with turning away from the tendencies

48
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.875
that pull us downward.

49
00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:47.333
In life

50
00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:51.666
there will always be something to provoke.

51
00:02:51.666 --> 00:02:55.625
Some person, some desire, some moment,

52
00:02:55.625 --> 00:02:58.791
that wants to pull you off the path.

53
00:02:58.791 --> 00:03:03.166
But remember – lust, anger,

54
00:03:03.166 --> 00:03:08.000
and greed are gateways, not bondages.

55
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.916
You are free within.

56
00:03:10.916 --> 00:03:15.083
The choice is yours – to step through them,

57
00:03:15.083 --> 00:03:19.041
or to step away.

58
00:03:19.041 --> 00:03:21.500
You cannot control outer

59
00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.250
circumstances, but

60
00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:28.291
you can choose your response.

61
00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:33.125
When you hold back the pull of lust,

62
00:03:33.125 --> 00:03:37.708
when you pause before reacting in anger,

63
00:03:37.708 --> 00:03:42.583
when you choose contentment over greed,

64
00:03:42.583 --> 00:03:47.250
you protect your peace

65
00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:51.833
and give strength to your soul.

66
00:03:51.833 --> 00:03:56.750
This is where life begins to feel lighter.

67
00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.916
Challenges do not end,

68
00:03:59.916 --> 00:04:06.666
but you no longer carry the weight
of inner storms.

69
00:04:06.666 --> 00:04:09.166
Step away from those gateways.

70
00:04:09.166 --> 00:04:12.166
You will find that I am

71
00:04:12.166 --> 00:04:15.916
standing there, holding another door open.

72
00:04:15.916 --> 00:04:21.916
The path of shreyah, the path of true wellbeing.

73
00:04:21.916 --> 00:04:23.958
To come to Me,

74
00:04:23.958 --> 00:04:27.916
you do not need to do something great.

75
00:04:27.916 --> 00:04:32.208
Simply stop feeding what

76
00:04:32.208 --> 00:04:35.166
takes you away from Me.

77
00:04:39.666 --> 00:04:42.833
Everyone wants peace in the home,

78
00:04:42.833 --> 00:04:45.666
safety, and love.

79
00:04:45.666 --> 00:04:51.583
But where anger's fire is continuously fuelled,

80
00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:53.791
peace cannot remain.

81
00:04:53.791 --> 00:04:56.833
Where desire becomes selfish,

82
00:04:56.833 --> 00:04:59.000
love cannot bloom.

83
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:02.083
And where greed spreads,

84
00:05:02.083 --> 00:05:05.208
trust cannot hold steady.

85
00:05:05.208 --> 00:05:08.833
This is why I said – kama, that is,

86
00:05:08.833 --> 00:05:12.833
lust, krodha, and lobha,

87
00:05:12.833 --> 00:05:14.708
do not only afflict you,

88
00:05:14.708 --> 00:05:18.458
they afflict those closest to you too.

89
00:05:18.458 --> 00:05:23.791
A single harsh sentence spoken in anger

90
00:05:23.791 --> 00:05:27.125
can break years of trust.

91
00:05:27.125 --> 00:05:28.083
A selfish

92
00:05:28.083 --> 00:05:32.250
demand can weaken family unity.

93
00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:36.083
A small greed can quietly eat away

94
00:05:36.083 --> 00:05:39.458
the closeness within the home.

95
00:05:39.458 --> 00:05:42.916
Mutual trust is like a beautiful figure

96
00:05:42.916 --> 00:05:47.208
moulded in clay.

97
00:05:47.208 --> 00:05:49.208
The stone of a harsh word

98
00:05:49.208 --> 00:05:51.791
shatters it.

99
00:05:51.791 --> 00:05:53.958
The blow of a selfish demand

100
00:05:53.958 --> 00:05:56.958
breaks it to pieces.

101
00:05:56.958 --> 00:05:58.250
The current of greed

102
00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:02.500
melts it away grain by grain.

103
00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:03.083
If you

104
00:06:03.083 --> 00:06:06.875
truly care for your family,

105
00:06:06.875 --> 00:06:11.333
giving them comfort and means is not enough.

106
00:06:11.333 --> 00:06:13.833
Protecting them from these inner

107
00:06:13.833 --> 00:06:17.958
enemies is equally necessary.

108
00:06:17.958 --> 00:06:21.708
When you hold back words of anger,

109
00:06:21.708 --> 00:06:25.208
when you share love without keeping score,

110
00:06:25.208 --> 00:06:29.125
when you release expectations,

111
00:06:29.125 --> 00:06:31.875
you do not lose anything,

112
00:06:31.875 --> 00:06:38.625
but you protect something very precious.

113
00:06:38.625 --> 00:06:40.458
This is

114
00:06:40.458 --> 00:06:43.791
the greatest gift you can give

115
00:06:43.791 --> 00:06:46.291
your family.

116
00:06:50.875 --> 00:06:54.458
You measure your progress by roles,

117
00:06:54.458 --> 00:06:58.375
results, and recognition.

118
00:06:58.375 --> 00:07:01.625
That is fine, but remember,

119
00:07:01.625 --> 00:07:06.083
I measure your progress by you
response to kama, that is,

120
00:07:06.083 --> 00:07:07.916
lust, krodha,

121
00:07:07.916 --> 00:07:10.083
and lobha.

122
00:07:10.083 --> 00:07:12.750
That is, anger and greed.

123
00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:18.166
You can rise to great heights in your profession,

124
00:07:18.166 --> 00:07:20.375
but if these three are still

125
00:07:20.375 --> 00:07:24.916
guiding your decisions,

126
00:07:24.916 --> 00:07:26.083
then you have grown

127
00:07:26.083 --> 00:07:28.708
only outwardly,

128
00:07:28.708 --> 00:07:30.416
not inwardly.

129
00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:34.333
I have called them the gateways of darkness

130
00:07:34.333 --> 00:07:35.125
because

131
00:07:35.125 --> 00:07:39.291
they do not always appear destructive.

132
00:07:39.291 --> 00:07:42.916
Sometimes they wear a suit.

133
00:07:42.916 --> 00:07:45.458
Sometimes they sit in meetings.

134
00:07:45.458 --> 00:07:49.125
Sometimes they fuel ambition.

135
00:07:49.125 --> 00:07:55.458
But behind the curtain, they
slowly erode peace, clarity,

136
00:07:55.458 --> 00:07:59.416
and purpose.

137
00:07:59.416 --> 00:08:03.375
True success is not only in achievements,

138
00:08:03.375 --> 00:08:05.791
but in what you become

139
00:08:05.791 --> 00:08:11.500
while achieving them.

140
00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:16.416
When you refuse the unjust path,

141
00:08:16.416 --> 00:08:20.375
when you respond with discernment

142
00:08:20.375 --> 00:08:23.166
rather than reaction,

143
00:08:23.166 --> 00:08:26.083
when you work not only for profit,

144
00:08:26.083 --> 00:08:29.875
but for meaning,

145
00:08:29.875 --> 00:08:31.833
then your soul too

146
00:08:31.833 --> 00:08:36.083
grows alongside your work.

147
00:08:36.083 --> 00:08:38.208
This is shreyah.

148
00:08:38.208 --> 00:08:40.375
True wellbeing.

149
00:08:40.375 --> 00:08:44.583
And when you choose this,

150
00:08:44.583 --> 00:08:45.583
then you progress

151
00:08:45.583 --> 00:08:49.958
not only in your organisation, but

152
00:08:49.958 --> 00:08:54.166
in My sight too.
